WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.580
How did one of the best selling fantasy authors&nbsp;
of the twenty-first century lose the adaptation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.260
opportunity of a lifetime? Just ask The&nbsp;
Kingkiller Chronicle’s Patrick Rothfuss.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.780
Fans of George R.R. Martin's fantasy series A&nbsp;
Song of Ice and Fire know just how torturous it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.940
is to wait for a forthcoming book in a series when&nbsp;
there's no release date in sight. That said, fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.320
of The Kingkiller Chronicle series might want to&nbsp;
have a word with those desperate Martin readers.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.080
Written by Patrick Rothfuss, The Kingkiller&nbsp;
Chronicle hit shelves in 2007 with its first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.300
installment, The Name of the Wind. Book 2, The&nbsp;
Wise Man's Fear, followed that up in 2011 after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.580
an extended but reasonable delay. However, the&nbsp;
third book, The Doors of Stone, is still nowhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:47.040
to be found. As of early 2023, readers have been&nbsp;
waiting for well over a decade for the celebrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.780
saga to come to a close, with essentially no&nbsp;
information about when that conclusion will come.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.240
In case you're not one of&nbsp;
this series' devoted fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.620
The Kingkiller Chronicle is set in the world&nbsp;
of Temerant and told primarily through the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.760
character's oral history as he recounts&nbsp;
it to a historian known as "chronicler."

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.080
The main character, Kvothe might be a&nbsp;
simple innkeeper in the story's present day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.580
but he was an accomplished wizard and&nbsp;
musician known by many ominous names in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.600
the past. In The Name of the Wind, Kvothe&nbsp;
tells the story of his tragic childhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.700
and his time spent in cities ravaged by&nbsp;
crime, eventually arriving at a heralded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.200
University where he begins to master a&nbsp;
variety of magical practices. The Wise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.820
Man's Fear follows Kvothe as his education&nbsp;
progresses and he travels to further corners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.900
of the world in his endless pursuit of the&nbsp;
legendary demonic group, the Chandrian.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.820
Between the over 1 million copies of The Name of&nbsp;
the Wind sold, The Wise Man's Fear reaching the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.560
top spot on the New York Times Bestseller list,&nbsp;
and the Game of Thrones-driven fantasy craze of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.640
the mid 2010s, it's not at all surprising&nbsp;
that Hollywood moved fairly quickly to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.500
an adaptation off the ground. In the summer of&nbsp;
2013, it was reported that a group of writers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.760
and producers had optioned the project, but&nbsp;
the rights expired after a couple of years.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.600
Enter Hamilton scribe and Pulitzer&nbsp;
Prize winner Lin-Manuel Miranda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.660
As a self-proclaimed megafan of Rothfuss' work,&nbsp;
Miranda was set to produce a TV series based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.380
The Kingkiller Chronicle. This seemed&nbsp;
to mean only good things for Rothfuss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.360
as fresh off the mania aroused by Hamilton,&nbsp;
Miranda was the hottest commodity in the industry.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.560
Miranda, who was reportedly also going&nbsp;
to write original music for the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.820
was effusive with his praise for The&nbsp;
Kingkiller Chronicle books. He told Vulture,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.780
"I think fans of good writing just like&nbsp;
The Name of the Wind. I had not read a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.640
of fantasy books at that point, but I read the&nbsp;
first sentence and I just, I was very drawn in."

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.680
Speaking to Entertainment Weekly, Miranda&nbsp;
also said his experience appearing in HBO's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.420
His Dark Materials helped him understand The&nbsp;
Kingkiller Chronicle better. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:47.040
the solution for how best to approach the&nbsp;
adaptation eluded even Miranda's sharp mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.380
and he left the project in 2022.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:54.060
Rothfuss has been elusive about the third book&nbsp;
in the promised trilogy for a while — to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.380
point that many fans doubt the series will ever&nbsp;
reach a conclusion. In fact, his own editor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.240
Betsy Wollheim, wrote in a Facebook post that she&nbsp;
hadn't read a word of Rothfuss' work in years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.780
sowing more seeds of doubt about the&nbsp;
trajectory for the book's release.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:12.720
What's more, as a Reddit user summarized in Summer&nbsp;
2022, Rothfuss also raised money for his charity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:19.260
by promising to release a new chapter from The&nbsp;
Doors of Stone by February 2022. As of early 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:24.060
the chapter has yet to materialize and Rothfuss&nbsp;
has yet to make any formal announcements as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.720
to why, which may do some harm to his&nbsp;
credibility in the eyes of producers.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.380
Rothfuss has, however, addressed&nbsp;
his lack of punctuality a few times.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.240
"You can't be more irritated about&nbsp;
not finishing this thing than me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.440
or my publisher. You got — at&nbsp;
best, you're third in line."

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.720
It's worth noting that Rothfuss pretty much&nbsp;
entered the Sci-Fi/Fantasy scene with The Name of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.880
the Wind, and he probably didn't expect his first&nbsp;
two books to blow up as much as they did. Unlike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.800
authors like George R.R. Martin, who has been&nbsp;
writing consistently for decades, Rothfuss doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.480
have the longstanding reputation that might&nbsp;
pacify fans regarding long delays in his writing.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.260
It's also worth acknowledging that&nbsp;
Rothfuss has released two Kingkiller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.460
novellas in the time since The Wise&nbsp;
Man's Fear came out, so fans can rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.240
assured the universe has not been sitting&nbsp;
stagnantly since the release of book two.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.660
It's likely that after Game of Thrones&nbsp;
outstripped its source material,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.220
Hollywood might be more liable to look&nbsp;
askance at unfinished series. Miranda's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.000
departure may not mark the end of the road for&nbsp;
The Kingkiller Chronicle's Hollywood journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.900
but it may be the end until the author&nbsp;
produces a concluding installment.

